<title>UK: Compass active amid placing talk.</title>
<headline>Compass active amid placing talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in catering group Compass Group Plc dropped in active trading on Tuesday amid talk that brokerage ABN AMRO Hoare Govett had placed a block of some six million shares in the market, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 8p at 612 by 1054 GMT in volume of 7.0 million.</p>
<p>No-one at Hoare Govett was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Traders pointed out that Accor Group of France held a stake of some 74 million shares or 23 percent in Compass.</p>
<p>Accor in Paris had no immediate comment on today's activity in Compass stock.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
